parameters.how_chosen:
Two rationales are given:
- physical: 'about walking pace' (spec L91-92; config.yaml L100-101);
- empirical: 'The rate was chosen by a sweep: faster growth lets neighbours a body-height apart become plausible within half a second, after which appearance noise decides between identical people' (spec L93-95).

The sweep claim has a single source. README L183-184, written in the same commit, says 'chosen by a sweep on this protocol (the design record says so)', and manuscript lines 621-622 copy it.

No command, value grid, scenario, seed list or output survives in git, docs/, paper_materials/ or any transcript. The 0fd1e04 commit message does not mention a sweep, and neither does the plan's step list (plan L11-27; 'Measure' is 'ablation, phantoms, relocate, pipeline, badge tables'). The crosscheck classed it DOC-ONLY (D189).

Post-hoc probe on 2026-10-04 (verification, seeds 0-2, uniform, default configs), enhanced recall and false merge:
- 0.02: 12/12, 0.0%;
- 0.04: 12/12, 0.0%;
- 0.05: 7/12 (58%), 4.6%;
- 0.06: 2/12 (17%), 4.6%.

The seed-free replay in this verification reproduces that cliff exactly: re-entries with a second plausible vacated worker number 0/4, 0/4, 1/4 and 3/4 at those speeds.

At gap 12 the true worker's radius is 0.5 + 0.03 x 13 = 0.89 h, because dt = gap+1 (see gate_horizon). The other vacated workers have radii 0.53-0.77 and lie at least 0.93 h away. 0.03 therefore sits about one probe step below a collapse on this exact geometry.
